<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Tampere</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1918</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finnish-civil-war">Finnish Civil War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tampere">Tampere</a> was the decisive battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finnish-civil-war">Finnish Civil War</a>, fought in March and April 1918. The White army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carl-gustaf-emil-mannerheim">Carl Gustaf Emil Mannerheim</a> besieged the Red-held industrial city of Tampere and took it after heavy street fighting on 6 April 1918, capturing about 11,000 Red Guards. The defeat broke the Reds' main front, and the Whites, aided by German troops who took Helsinki, won the war in May.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-tampere.jpg" alt="Battle of Tampere" width="320" height="204" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tampere_destroyed_in_Civil_War.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
